 ": every ray from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"41f6ddbf-3160-4ee4-9b51-7aaf6526f202"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ray from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is a shortest path ",
 StyleBox["(p = v\:2080, \[Ellipsis], v\:2099)", "TI"],
 " whose end has no neighbour ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["d(p, u) = n + 1", "TI"],
 ". The ray from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " is the family of the rays from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that pass through ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"157b8a92-117e-4632-8756-58d73d4b5453"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A vertex ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " lies on the ray when it lies between ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", or beyond ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["d(p, e) = d(p, q) + d(q, e)", "TI"],
 ". On the square grid the part beyond ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " is a quadrant when ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " is off the axes of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", and a half-plane when ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " is on one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"67bdcde9-ce87-421f-b955-447bfa37b11b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ray ends where ",
 StyleBox["d(p, \[CenterDot])", "TI"],
 " has a local maximum. Rays with different ends can have different lengths. \
The ends of the pencil at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " are all the local maxima of ",
 StyleBox["d(p, \[CenterDot])", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b007aa6d-bee3-4a95-b60a-6275b1c7fdd5"],

